posts.body:
BB45 said:
But I am still missing the conditional branch
If：Player(x) is affected by off-balance
as I have two players on screen
Click to expand...
The notetag instructions should say you're provided with a
user
variable to represent the battler getting (or losing) the state.
So to check which actor ID is being affected, you do this inside the notetag:
Code:
if (user.actorId() == 2)
{
// script call to erase actor ID 2's picture
// script call to draw actor ID 2's off-balance picture
}
else
{
// script call to erase the other actor's picture
// script call to draw the other actor's off-balance picture
}
Then the notetag for when the state is removed, obviously you just reverse which pictures are being erased and drawn.

@ATT_Turan
Sorry to bother you again but I have decided to add another condition into my notetag, which is a switch that must be turned on before the picture changes are applied.
Code:
<JS On Add State>
if (target.actorId() == 2 && $gameSwitches.setValue(6, true));
{
$gameScreen.erasePicture(1);
$gameScreen.showPicture(1, 'Mel_KnockedDown', 0, 248, 456, 100, 100, 255, 0);
}
</JS On Add State>
I think I am using the wrong script call as it only just "sets" the switch to on/off but I couldn't find any other script call that is actually "checking" a switch.
I have seen however, in another post for the RGSS engine, that someone used
if $Game_Switches[103] == true
but to no surprise this did not work in MZ.
